{
  "note": "Every disagreement parser_agreement.py has found and not yet resolved, with the exact groups observed. The suite fails if a split appears that is not here, or one listed here heals or changes shape. Fix the language or the parser, then delete the entry; do not edit groups by hand to make a run pass.",
  "reasons": {
    "java-defect": "Java classifies a legal token in the wrong place as misbound; the forge, and syntax.py, call it unbounded. Doctrine (PIPELINE.md) only rules on running out of input (unbounded) and an illegal character (misbound); this case is unratified.",
    "earley-where": "On input that ends too soon, P1-P3 refuse at the end of input; P4 (Earley) and P5 (generated from GRAMMAR.ebnf) refuse at the last token. Same verdict, different place. The forge's own laws only check that a refusal points inside the text, so it never saw this.",
    "unterminated": "syntax.py's MASTER regex never matches an unclosed string, so its 'unterminated string' (unbounded) branch is dead code and it reports misbound for an unexpected character instead. ratified.json rules unbounded.",
    "superset": "syntax.py accepts the v4.10 statement language on top of the core (let/ever statements, not, mixed defs and expressions) and repairs punctuation (Recovery). Expected by design; listed so it stays visible.",
    "empty": "syntax.py accepts an empty program as an empty Program; every other witness refuses it as unbounded."
  },
